SUMMARY:Occidental Ukulele Fest!
DESCRIPTION:Saturday April 25 at 10 am – 8:30 pm. Occidental Ukulele Fest! at Occidental Center for the Arts. Join us for Occidental’s First Annual Ukulele Festival! Musicians of all experience levels are welcome at this inclusive event. With a festival ticket you’ll enjoy: workshops and jams\, performances including evening headliner George Kahumoku \,local Ukulele Clubs’ networking\, Open Mic\, and more! You will also be able to join a special\, optional workshop with George Kahumoku (separate fee applies for the workshop). Don’t miss this fun fest for Ukulele players and enthusiasts! Please check out schedule details at www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org. This event is sponsored by Warming Trends of Sonoma County. Tickets are $50 for the festival\, $40 for OCA members at www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org. . Morning snacks\, lunch and dinner will be offered for sale on-site. You may also walk to downtown Occidental where there are several options (about 3 blocks away from OCA). Free parking is available. 3850 Doris Murphy Ct. Occidental\, CA. 95465. OCA is a community-based non-profit arts organization with volunteer staffing for events.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/occidental-ukulele-fest/
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Ct.\, Occidental
CATEGORIES:Music
GEO:38.41055;-122.95024
